ode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1198496-bjd-dhampire-questions?p=1407136#post1407136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. No the Dhampire generally age slower after having his Vampire side awaken during puperty though it is not clarified how much slower.<br /> 2. No the Dhampire is only created from having sex with 15+ Vampire and a mortal. Dhampire with Revenant would only mayby create another Revenant though it is more likely to be just another normal human.<br /> 3. Yes and Yes. This whas retconed from TotTB where a Dhampire could still like a ghoul raise his disciples by drinking low gen blood. Now you still can only have one Dot and it even cost as much as a ghoul despite getting less freebies. I would personally Houserule that because Dhampires are more vampire then human they pay like other vampires only EXP for each new disciple (or mayby 10 like a new sphere for a mage).<br /> 4. Yes, their Blood is even thinner then those of a 15 or 16th Gen Vampire so for them every vampire boon or bain is impossible.<br /> <br /> Well I have another question. If a male vampire have sex during getting mortal for a day with a disciple like &quot;The greatest Trick&quot; from Mytherica or &quot;Necromancy&quot; can he then creates children and if yes, is it then a normal mortal or a Dhampire?</div> </div> </div> </div>For #2, technically there's a precedent for the kids of dhampires to be revenants by default. There's an african bloodline with a clan curse that they can only feed off a specific revenant bloodline, the origins of which are a dhampir created between their bloodline founder and a mortal woman sorcerer.<br /> <br /> That also sets a precedent for any children a vampire has to be dhampires, whether it's using &quot;greatest trick&quot; or &quot;the corpse in the monster&quot; path of necromancy. That kinda makes sense, the legends of dhampires existing are a Lot older than modern nights.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of dhampires having normal XP cost for disciplines with ghoul discipline limits. In legends, dhampires said to hunt their immortal parents, so making it so they brogress by hunting vamps seems thematic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 08-11-2020, 12:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}